Reading Multi-Line CSV Files in Apache Spark 

When dealing with multi-line CSV files (where a single record spans multiple lines), you need to enable the multiLine option while reading the file using Spark DataFrame API. 

 
 

✅ Solution: Using multiLine option in Spark 

python 

from pyspark.sql import SparkSession 

  

# Initialize Spark session 

spark = SparkSession.builder.appName("MultiLineCSV").getOrCreate() 

  

# Read the multi-line CSV file 

df = spark.read.option("header", "true") \ 

               .option("multiLine", "true") \ 

               .option("quote", '"') \   # Handles quoted newlines properly 

               .option("escape", "\\") \ # Escapes special characters 

               .csv("path/to/your_file.csv") 

  

df.show(truncate=False) 

 

 

 
 

📌 Key Options Explained 

Option 

Purpose 

"header", "true" 

Treats the first row as column names. 

"multiLine", "true" 

Allows Spark to read records that span multiple lines. 

"quote", '"' 

Ensures fields enclosed in double quotes are read correctly. 

"escape", "\\" 

Handles escape characters properly. 

 
 

🚀 Example CSV File (multi-line record) 

cs 

CopyEdit 

id,name,description 1,John Doe,"Software Engineer working on AI" 2,Jane Smith,"Data Scientist specializing in ML"  

✅ Expected Output 

pgsql 

CopyEdit 

+---+-----------+----------------------------+ |id |name |description | +---+-----------+----------------------------+ |1 |John Doe |Software Engineer working on AI | |2 |Jane Smith |Data Scientist specializing in ML | +---+-----------+----------------------------+  

 
 

⚠️ Common Issues & Fixes 

Malformed records? → Use .option("mode", "DROPMALFORMED") or "PERMISSIVE". 

Performance issues? → Multi-line parsing is slower; consider increasing partition size. 

Quote issues? → Ensure proper double quotes (") wrapping text fields. 

 
 

🔥 Performance Tip 

If reading large CSV files, increase the executor memory and parallelism: 

spark.conf.set("spark.sql.files.maxPartitionBytes", "128MB")  

 

  

